WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.063
- All right.

00:00:01.063 --> 00:00:01.896
You know it, and I know it,

00:00:01.896 --> 00:00:04.190
sometimes this world can
be a little upside down

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.130
and that's why I love
that here on this show

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.080
we can be a vessel to
share fun and positivity.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.550
So from time to time we
look back at all our shows

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.233
to bring you mash up moments we love.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.223
So today it's all about the crazy jobs

00:00:19.223 --> 00:00:22.160
our celebrity guests have
had before they were stars.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:22.993
Check it out.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.413
What was your first real job?

00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:28.000
- I worked in a fish and chip shop.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.390
I was the potato peeler.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.890
- Were you a runner in a recording studio?

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.520
- Amongst other things, yeah.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.640
- I'm a fourth generation dog shower.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.430
Yeah. There's me at some of the dog shows.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.948
- I worked at the Bronx zoo for a summer.

00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:40.430
- I worked at the Fort Worth zoo.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.263
- Really?

00:00:41.263 --> 00:00:42.096
- Yes, for a summer.

00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:42.929
- Oh my goodness.

00:00:42.929 --> 00:00:45.320
- I used to work at the Four
Seasons hotel in Beverly Hills.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.170
I waited on anywhere from Nicole Kidman,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.370
to Al Pacino, to Robert De Niro.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.203
So yeah.

00:00:52.203 --> 00:00:53.440
- I bet you all of them were
waiters at some point too.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.540
I feel like we all were waitress.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.480
Were you a good waiter?

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.680
- I was not only a waiter,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.205
I was selling satellite dishes...

00:00:59.205 --> 00:01:02.130
- (Kelly laughs)

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.330
- Out of a kiosk in the ghetto. So, uh.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.550
- I sold vacuum cleaners for two days.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.383
- Is that right?

00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:09.540
- Uh-huh, and I was like, I'm out.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.834
Mm-hm, yeah, I couldn't do it.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.170
- We all had these jobs. - Yeah.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.200
- I used to glaze ham at Honey Baked Ham.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.680
- Oh my gosh, those are good!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.689
- Honey Baked Ham! Look.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:20.470
- Those are good.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.080
We get those for like
Christmas and Thanksgiving.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.930
I'm not kidding, they're so good.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:25.763
- Yeah, I glazed them.

00:01:25.763 --> 00:01:26.960
- Nicely done. - Yeah.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:27.950
- You are great at glazing. - Thank you.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.603
- See? It's all this that
builds to where you are now.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:33.250
- And when I was like, yeah,
I'm gonna tweet Marvel,

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.083
and it's gonna be great.

00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:35.570
They're gonna, you know, read the tweet

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.799
get back to me, offer me a role.

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:37.632
- Mm-hm.

00:01:37.632 --> 00:01:39.350
- I also just kind of
picked up like, you know,

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.230
weird modeling gigs whenever I could.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:42.800
And like, oh, when I say modeling

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.380
I'm not I'm, I wasn't
like a runway Prada model.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.560
I was like, I was like a
stock, you know, stock photos.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.850
- Wait, like when you
buy the picture frame?

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.652
- Like when you, when you buy
the picture frame exactly.

00:01:52.652 --> 00:01:54.270
Or like when you go on a website.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.650
- I always think those
families are so beautiful.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:57.620
I'm like sometimes yeah,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.590
I, yeah,

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.277
I'm like, well done if
they cast you for that.

00:02:01.277 --> 00:02:04.730
- Yeah. The one I did like a
couple of shoots and they ended

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.330
up like, I literally
keep seeing it pop up,

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.730
and like more so now 'cause
people are recognizing them.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.790
- So tell us about your motivation
in some of these photos.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.330
What's happening here?

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.163
- Oh man.

00:02:16.163 --> 00:02:17.600
- It's the merger? You're
discussing the merger?

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.433
- There's the merger.

00:02:18.433 --> 00:02:19.300
There's a merger, Kelly.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.336
Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:21.336 --> 00:02:22.773
There's a lot going on in this, guys.

00:02:22.773 --> 00:02:25.523
A lot of really, really
intense character work.

00:02:25.523 --> 00:02:26.356
- Yeah.

00:02:26.356 --> 00:02:28.350
- You know, I see my
two colleagues over here

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.030
they're studying an annual report, right?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.218
And I, over there leaning over
the the head of the table.

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:34.051
- Yeah.

00:02:34.051 --> 00:02:35.870
And, and leading this meeting, all right?

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.960
- Yes. A leader.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:37.900
You look like a leader.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.820
- Thank you. - Yeah.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.653
- Thank you. I appreciate that.

00:02:39.653 --> 00:02:41.530
- If that was what the
motivation was, you nailed it.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.363
